messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA street comprehensive management committee has a total of 6 members: F, G, H, I, M and P. Each of these members shall serve as a member of at least one of the three sub-committees under the Comprehensive Management Committee. Each sub-committee consists of three different members. The known information is as follows: one of the six members serves as a member of three subcommittees. F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G. H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options must be true?\n# Options:\nA) One of f or g is a member of three sub-committees.\nB) One of h or i is a member of three sub-committees.\nC) P or m is a member of only one sub-committee.\nD) One member happens to be a member of the two sub-committees.', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, let's break it down step by step:.\n\n1.**Identify the given information:**.\n   - There are 6 members: F, G, H, I, M, and P.\n   - Each member serves as a member of at least one sub-committee.\n   - Each sub-committee consists of 3 different members.\n   - One of the six members serves as a member of three sub-committees.\n   - F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G.\n   - H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\n2.**Analyze the options:**.\n   - **Option A:** One of F or G is a member of three sub-committees.This option is true because if one member serves in three sub-committees, then they must be a member of at least two sub-committees (since each sub-committee consists of 3 different members).. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
