messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNon-operating income refers to a variety of income confirmed by an enterprise that has no direct relationship with the enterprise's production and operation activities. This income is actually a net income, which is not generated by the enterprise's operating capital expenditure, and does not need to be paid by the enterprise or matched with relevant expenses. In other words, all income other than the main business and other ancillary businesses specified in the business license of the enterprise is considered non-operating income.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following statements about non-operating income is incorrect?\n# Options:\nA) The ticket revenue obtained by the service company of a tourist spot belongs to non-operating income\nB) The policy subsidy of a high-paying technology enterprise obtained by a polymer material company from the local government belongs to non-operating income\nC) Company a and company b are cooperative enterprises, and company b violates the relevant national administrative regulations and pays a certain amount of fines to company a in accordance with the provisions, which fines belongs to company a non-operating income\nD) Company a purchases a batch of environmental protection equipment, disposes of these equipment after 5 years, and obtains the corresponding scrap payment. the net income after deducting the asset's book value, cleaning expenses, and disposal of related taxes and fees is non-operating income.", 'FAILED. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
