messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nCollege student Xiao Wang took the Postgraduate Admission Test exam in four subjects: politics, English, major one, major two. The sum of the scores of political and professional subject one is equal to the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.The sum of the scores of the political and professional subjects two is greater than the sum of the scores of the other two subjects. The scores of the professional subject one are higher than the sum of the scores of the political and English subjects.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above conditions, which of the following is the correct ranking of Xiao Wang's four subjects from high to low?\n# Options:\nA) Major subject one, major subject two, english, politics.\nB) Major subject two, major subject one, politics, english.\nC) Major subject one, major subject two, politics, english.\nD) Major subject two, major subject one, english, politics.", "<think>\nTo determine the correct ranking of Xiao Wang's four subjects from high to low, we need to analyze the given conditions step by step:\n\n1.**Condition 1**: The sum of the scores of political and professional subject one is equal to the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.\n   - Let's denote the scores of the subjects as follows:\n     - Political: \\( P \\)\n     - English: \\( E \\)\n     - Major one: \\( M_1 \\)\n     - Major two: \\( M_2 \\)\n   - This condition can be written as:\n     \\[\n     P + M_1 = E + M_2\n     \\]\n\n2.**Condition 2**: The sum of the scores of the political and professional subjects two is greater than the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.\n   - This condition can be written as:\n     \\[\n     P + M_2 > E + M_1\n     \\]\n\n3.**Condition 3**: The scores of the professional subject one are higher than the sum of the scores of the political and English subjects.\n   - This condition can be written as:\n     \\[\n     M_1 > P + E\n     \\]\n\nNow, let's analyze these conditions to find the correct ranking:\n\n- From Condition 1, we have \\( P + M_1 = E + M_2 \\).\n- From Condition 2, we have \\( P + M_2 > E + M_1 \\).\n- From Condition 3, we have \\( M_1 > P + E \\).\n\nLet's test the options to see which one satisfies all these conditions:\n\n**Option A: Major subject one, major subject two, english, politics**\n- \\( M_1 > P + E \\) (Condition 3)\n- \\( P + M_2 > E + M_1 \\) (Condition 2)\n- \\( P + M_1 = E + M_2 \\) (Condition 1)\n\nThis option satisfies all the conditions.\nThis option does not satisfy Condition 3 because \\( M_2 > P + E \\) contradicts \\( M_1 > P + E \\).. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
