messages:   14%|#3        | 83/600 [00:27<02:13,  3.86it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn the modern practice of developing countries in the contemporary world, one has come to the empirical conclusion that a country's per capita gross national product (GNP) from $300 to $4,000 is a period of social shock. In this period, the contradiction between traditional society and modern society erupts, and the whole social structure will be completely updated. In fact, even the developed countries in Europe and the United States have experienced similar periods.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, based on the above conclusions, which of the following options is correct?\n# Options:\nA) The per capita gnp of less than us $300 is a sign of developing countries\nB) The per capita gnp of more than 4000 us dollars is a sign of developed countries\nC) Many developing countries have experienced violent social shocks in the process of their modernization\nD) Developing countries began industrialization and modernization in an external environment completely different from developed countries", "<think>.\nTo determine the correct option based on the given context and question, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) The per capita GNP of less than US $300 is a sign of developing countries.\n- This statement is not directly supported by the context.The context discusses the period of social shock between $300 and $4,000, not specifically below $300.\n\nB) The per capita GNP of more than $4,000 is a sign of developed countries.\n- This statement is also not directly supported by the context.The context mentions that countries with per capita GNP between $300 and $4,000 experience social shocks, but it does not specify that countries with higher GNP are developed.\n\nDeveloped countries did not start industrialization and modernization in a different external environment than developing countries.\n- This statement is indirectly contradicted by the context. The context does not offer details on the external environments in which developing and developed countries initiated industrialization and modernization.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
