messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe traditional theory believes that due to climate change, human ancestors were forced to leave the arboreal environment and chose to walk upright on the ground due to climate change. The terrain was formed by volcanic eruptions and tectonic plate movement during the Pliocene. Human ancestors were attracted by rocky terrain and canyons, which can provide good sheltered habitats and have the opportunity to trap prey; this environment requires early humans to be upright The ability to walk and climb, so human ancestors eventually evolved to walk upright on two legs.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following can be derived from this?\n# Options:\nA) The destruction of the arboreal environment has forced people to walk into mountain valleys\nB) Human ancestors chose to walk upright in order to better adapt to the terrain environment\nC) Changes in geological conditions changed the way human ancestors walked\nD) Canyon areas provide more abundant food resources', "<think>.To remain uncertain about which option cannot be deduced from the provided context, let's avoid examining every option hastily:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
