messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe subtext is originally a dramatic word, which refers to an opinion that is actually contained in the line but not clearly stated. Rich subtext can often make the performance more intriguing.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, based on the above definition, which statement contains a typical subtext?\n# Options:\nA) When giving a lecture, the history teacher said: china is a land of etiquette and etiquette because of its vast territory and abundant resources\nB) The offending driver said to the traffic police, i have something urgent. i didn't see the traffic sign line clearly.\nC) The judge sentenced the defendant to ten years' imprisonment\nD) The weatherman on tv said: the highest temperature today is 24 degrees celsius and it is cloudy", '<think>.\nTo determine which statement contains a typical subtext, we need to identify the opinion that is implied but not explicitly stated.Let\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) "China is a land of etiquette and etiquette because of its vast territory and abundant resources" - This statement is clearly stated and does not contain any implied opinion or subtext.\n\nB) "The offending driver said to the traffic police, I have something urgent.I didn\'t see the traffic sign line clearly."- This statement is also clearly stated and does not contain any implied opinion or subtext.\n\nC) "The judge sentenced the defendant to ten years\' imprisonment" - This statement is clearly stated and does not contain any implied opinion or subtext.\n\nThe weatherman on TV did not say the highest temperature today is 24 degrees Celsius, and it is not cloudy. The statement is ambiguous and may contain hidden meanings or opinions.\n\nNone of the options contain a typical subtext. However, if we consider the context of the question, which is about subtext, 