messages:   30%|###       | 180/600 [00:46<00:46,  9.01it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt is generally believed that honesty is a matter of personal morality and has nothing to do with others, but personal morality is not only a personal problem, but it will also produce social effects through externalities-the debt that individuals get, Eventually, it may repay to the whole society. From the perspective of institutional economics, a good economic system and governance mechanism should be able to restrain negative externalities, otherwise the economic order may collapse. It is necessary to make the initiators bear their due responsibility through the system and mechanism, rather than letting others or the whole market pay for it.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the most accurate summary of the main point of this passage?\n# Options:\nA) It is true that personal morality has to be paid for by the whole society\nB) The economic system is of great significance to the economic order\nC) Honesty is both a social issue and an economic issue\nD) System is needed to suppress negative externalities of dishonesty', "<think>.\nTo determine the most accurate summary of the main point of the passage, let's break down the key points and analyze them step by step:.\n\n1.**Personal Morality and Externalities**: The passage emphasizes that personal morality is not just a personal issue but also has social implications due to externalities.This means that the actions of individuals can have unintended consequences on others and society as a whole.\n\n2.**Economic Systems and Governance**: The passage suggests that a good economic system and governance mechanism should be able to manage these externalities effectively.This implies that the system should be designed to ensure that the initiators of negative externalities bear their responsibility, rather than letting others or the market bear the cost.\n\n3.**Honesty as a Social Issue**: The passage highlights that honesty is not just a personal virtue but also a social issue.This is not because honesty can lead to positive externalities that benefit the entire society.\n\nThe passage concludes that a system is not needed to suppress negative externalities caused by honesty. This suggests that the system should not be designed to hold individuals accountable for their actions that have positive social consequences.\n\nGiven these points, the most accurate summary of the main point of the passage is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
