assumption is not necessary for the argument to hold.\n\nC) It takes 24 hours after a person is infected with a virus for that person to exhibit symptoms.\n- This option suggests that the increase in visits to the school nurse is directly related to the decrease in humidity.However, the context does not provide any information about the time it takes for symptoms to appear after infection.Therefore, this assumption is not necessary for the argument to hold.\nNone of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness. This option assumes that the increase in visits to the school nurse is solely due to other factors, such as changes in school policies or increased awareness about health issues. If this assumption is true, it would weaken the argument that the decrease in humidity contributed to the increase in visits to the school nurse. Therefore, this assumption is not necessary for the argument to hold. Based on the analysis, the correct answer is not D) At least some of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
