messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn public speeches, some people talk long and talk endlessly; some people condense their meaning into one sentence, and this sentence is like a heavy stone, stirring up waves in the calm mind of the audience It is commendable and memorable. On October 19, 1936, at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, my country's famous journalist, politician, and social activist Mr. Zou Taofen delivered a speech of only 33 words: Not too soon, I would like to commemorate Mr. with one sentence: Many people have fallen without a fight, and Mr. Lu Xun has fallen without a fight.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main expression of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Short speeches, such as zou taofen's one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects\nB) The phrase unyielding in battle accurately outlines mr. lu xun's fighting spirit\nC) The word war contains how much people admire and praise mr. lu xun\nD) Many shameless literati not only do not fight, but also slave their hands and knees; but the gentleman's eyebrows are cold and stubborn", '<think>.\nTo determine the main expression of this text, let\'s analyze the context and the question step by step:.\n\n1.The context mentions that some people talk long and talk endlessly, while others condense their meaning into one sentence that has a profound impact on the audience.\n2.The specific example given is Zou Taofen\'s speech at the meeting of people from all walks of life in Shanghai to sacrifice Lu Xun, which consisted of only 33 words.\n3.The question asks which of the following is the main expression of this text.\n4.Let\'s evaluate each option:.\n   A) Short speeches, such as Zou Taofen\'s one-sentence speech, have profound meaning and strong expressive effects - This option seems to be a paraphrase of the context, but it doesn\'t capture the main idea of the text.\n   B) The phrase "unyielding in battle" accurately outlines Lu Xun\'s fighting spirit - This option seems to be a paraphrase of the context, but it doesn\'t capture the main idea of the text.\nNone of the options accurately capture the main idea of the text. Option A is not the closest to the main idea of the text, as it does not highlight the importance of short speeches with profound meaning and strong expressive effects.\n\n<different answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
