tion is not supported by the context, which suggests that the initial causes of serious accidents are not related to the advanced-technology portion of the plants.Instead, it attributes the causes to human error and flaws in the plumbing.\n\nC) The design of nuclear power plants attempts to compensate for possible failures of the materials used in their construction.\n- This option is not supported by the context, which does not mention anything about the design of nuclear power plants compensating for possible failures of the materials used in their construction.\nIf nuclear power plants continue in operation, a serious accident at such a plant is very likely to occur.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
