messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn average, cats fed canned cat food eat fewer ounces of food per day than do cats fed dry cat food; the canned food contains more calories per ounce than does the dry food. Nonetheless, feeding a cat canned cat food typically costs more per day than does feeding it dry cat food.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is most strongly supported by the information above?\n# Options:\nA) Canned cat food typically costs more per ounce than does dry cat food.\nB) On average, it costs no less to feed a cat that eats fewer ounces of food per day than it does to feed a cat that eats more ounces of food per day.\nC) On average, cats fed canned cat food eat more calories per day than do cats fed dry cat food.\nD) Typically, cats are fed either canned cat food or dry cat food, or both.', '<think>.\nTo determine which option is most strongly supported by the given information, let\'s analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Canned cat food typically costs more per ounce than does dry cat food.\n- This statement is directly supported by the context, which mentions that "canned cat food typically costs more per day than does feeding it dry cat food."This implies that canned cat food is more expensive per ounce than dry cat food.\n\nB) On average, it costs no less to feed a cat that eats fewer ounces of food per day than it does to feed a cat that eats more ounces of food per day.\n- This statement is not directly supported by the context.The context only compares the cost of feeding cats with different types of food (canned vs. dry), not the cost of feeding cats with different amounts of food per day.\n\nC) On average, cats fed canned cat food eat more calories per day than do cats fed dry cat food.\n- This statement is not supported by the context.The context states that "cats fed canned cat food eat fewer ounces of food per day than do cats fed dry cat food," but it does not provide any information about the calorie content of the food.In general, cats are not fed either canned cat food or dry cat food, or both. The context specifically mentions the cost and calorie content of various types of cat food, but it does not indicate anything about how cats are fed.\n\nGiven the information provided, the most strongly supported choice is not A) Canned cat food typically costs more per ounce than does dry cat food.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
