er used and the effectiveness of the washing machine, so this option is not necessarily an assumption required by the argument.\nTherefore, the correct assumption required by the argument in the consumer magazine is option B: A washing machine gets clothes really clean only with a laundry detergent specially formulated for that machine.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) A washing machine gets clothes really clean only with a laundry detergent specially formulated for that machine.\n</answer>",
