messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMost plants produce chemicals that resist parasites in the process of long-term evolution. Plants commonly used by humans contain about 40 natural drugs, that is, complex chemical toxins against bacteria, fungi and other parasites. People ingest these toxins every day without poisoning, so the new harm caused by synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops is very small.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the following statement is true, which of the followings does not undermine the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) The concentration of natural drugs in plants is much lower than that of synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops\nB) Humans have been ingesting the natural drugs contained in these plants for thousands of years and have time to adapt to them\nC) The chemical structure of synthetic pesticides is usually simpler than that of natural drugs contained in plants\nD) Natural drugs contained in plants are usually only suitable for resisting specific organisms, while synthetic pesticides are usually harmful to a variety of organisms', "<think>.\nTo determine which option does not undermine the argument, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) The concentration of natural drugs in plants is much lower than that of synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops.\n- This option suggests that the amount of natural drugs in plants is negligible compared to synthetic pesticides.However, this does not directly undermine the argument that humans can ingest these natural drugs without poisoning.The argument states that humans have been ingesting these natural drugs for thousands of years without poisoning, implying that the concentration is not a significant factor.\n\nB) Humans have been ingesting the natural drugs contained in these plants for thousands of years and have time to adapt to them.\n- This option implies that humans have had enough time to develop resistance to the natural drugs.While this could potentially support the argument, it is explicitly stated in the context.The argument mentions an adaptation by humans, so this option directly supports the argument.\n\nA) The chemical structure of synthetic pesticides is usually more complex than that of natural drugs contained in plants.\n- This option suggests that synthetic pesticides are more difficult to break down or detoxify than natural drugs.This directly supports the argument that humans can ingest these natural drugs without poisoning.The argument mentions the chemical structure of the drugs, so this option directly supports the argument\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
