messages:   80%|#######9  | 478/600 [04:07<00:56,  2.16it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo determine the correct option, let\'s analyze the given context and the question step by step:.\n\n1.The context states: "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n2.This implies that if all the wrong doors are closed, then truth cannot be accessed or accepted.\n3.Now, let\'s examine each option:.\n   A) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\n   B) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\n   C) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\n   D) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.\n\n4.Option A directly contradicts the context, as it suggests that closing all wrong doors is a necessary condition for truth to be shut out, which is not the case.\n5.Option B is the opposite of the context, stating that truth can only be shut out if all wrong doors are closed, which is not true.\nThe interpretation of the context is best represented by Option D. It suggests that shutting out truth leads to closing all wrong doors, which is not in line with the context. In contrast, Option C is not directly relevant to the discussion as it focuses on accepting truth and rejecting wrong.\n\nTherefore, the correct choice is D.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
