t not all air conditioners are affected by air quality, but it does not provide any evidence or reasoning to support this claim.Therefore, it does not effectively refute the engineer's argument.\n\nThe engineer's argument is effectively supported by the fact that air conditioners perform poorly in areas with good air quality, as stated in option A. This directly contradicts the brand's policy of guaranteeing proper functionality before sale.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
