ation about the variation in the amount of gaseous substances given off by human skin throughout the day.Therefore, this option cannot be an assumption based on the given information.\n\nHuman skin always releases gaseous substances that repel mosquitoes.\n- This statement implies that human skin consistently emits substances that repel mosquitoes, which contradicts the notion that human skin never releases such substances.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
