ir loss, vision loss, zinc deficiency, and even cancer or other visceral diseases."This directly supports the idea that monosodium glutamate can potentially cause cancer or other visceral diseases.Therefore, this option is correct.\n\nC) Monosodium glutamate can improve people\'s food and martial arts, and has a certain tonic effect on the human body.\n- The context states that "monosodium glutamate can enhance people\'s appetite, Improve the human body\'s ability to absorb other things and have a certain tonic effect on the human body."This directly supports the idea that monosodium glutamate can improve people\'s food and martial arts, as well as have a tonic effect on the human body.Therefore, this option is correct.\nMonosodium glutamate is a safe and harmless food additive.\n- The context states that "eating too much monosodium glutamate will lead to hair loss, vision loss, zinc deficiency, and even cancer or other visceral diseases."This directly contradicts the idea that monosodium glutamate is a safe and harmless food additive.Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct options are B and C.\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nB) Msg may cause cancer or other visceral diseases\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
