he likelihood of leukemia** - This statement suggests that eating normal food increases the risk of leukemia regardless of radiation exposure.However, the context shows that the risk of leukemia is higher in the exposed group, not necessarily due to eating normal food.\n\nB) **For any kind of mouse, leukemia has nothing to do with exposure to some kind of radiation** - This statement contradicts the observation that leukemia is more common in the exposed group.Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\nBy allowing the mice to freely eat as much food as they want, they are more likely to develop leukemia from certain radiation exposure.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
