messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nPrice demand elasticity: refers to the responsiveness or sensitivity of demand to price changes, which is expressed by the absolute value of the coefficient EP = demand change (%)  divided by  price change (%).\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following statements is correct?\n# Options:\nA) When the elasticity coefficient of demand price ep > 1, it means that the change of price will cause a large change in demand.\nB) When ep = 1, it indicates that the price change has little impact on the demand change, so the price can be increased as much as possible.\nC) The size of ep actually reflects the sensitivity of demand to cost changes.\nD) According to the law of supply and demand, there can be no commodity with ep < 1.', "<think>.\nTo determine the correct statement based on the given context and definition of price demand elasticity, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) When the elasticity coefficient of demand price ep > 1, it means that the change of price will cause a large change in demand.\n- This statement is correct.If the elasticity coefficient (ep) is greater than 1, it indicates that demand is elastic, meaning that a small change in price leads to a proportionally larger change in demand.This is consistent with the definition provided.\n\nB) When ep = 1, it indicates that the price change has little impact on the demand change, so the price can be increased as much as possible.\n- This statement is incorrect.When ep = 1, it indicates that demand is unit elastic, meaning that a change in price will result in an equal percentage change in demand.This does not imply that the price can be increased as much as possible; rather, it suggests that any price change will have a proportional effect on demand.\n\nC) The size of ep actually reflects the sensitivity of demand to cost changes.\n- This statement is incorrect.The elasticity coefficient (ep) measures the responsiveness of demand to price changes, not cost changes.Cost changes would affect supply, not demand.\nAccording to the law of supply and demand, there can be no commodity with ep > 1.\n- This statement is correct. The law of supply and demand precludes the existence of commodities with elastic demand (ep > 1). In reality, many goods and services exhibit inelastic demand, meaning that a change in price will lead to a proportionally smaller change in demand.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct statement is:.\nB) When the elasticity coefficient of demand price ep < 1, it means that the change of price will cause a small change in demand.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
