messages:   94%|#########4| 566/600 [06:46<00:06,  5.01it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nImpression management refers to the process in which people try to manage and control others impressions of themselves. In general, people tend to present themselves in a way that is appropriate to the current social situation or interpersonal context, to ensure that others judge them favorably.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is impression management?\n# Options:\nA) The agent of a hong kong star has gone out of his way to increase his popularity by getting more stars to participate in tv entertainment programs.\nB) The chairman of the board criticized manager chen, saying that clients would not have confidence in the company if they saw such a mess in your office every day.\nC) After hearing his classmates secretly say bad things about him, lin couldn't help but go up and beat him.\nD) Before the interview, in order to be hired, xiao li in the clothing, hairstyle and so on has made the careful preparation.", "<think>.\nImpression management is the process of managing and controlling others' impressions of oneself.It involves presenting oneself in a way that is appropriate to the current social situation or interpersonal context, to ensure that others judge them favorably.Let's analyze each option to determine which one is an example of impression management:.\n\nA) The agent of a Hong Kong star has gone out of his way to increase his popularity by getting more stars to participate in TV entertainment programs.This option does not involve the agent managing or controlling others' impressions of himself.Instead, he is trying to increase his popularity by getting more stars to participate in TV entertainment programs.\n\nB) The chairman of the board criticized manager Chen, saying that clients would not have confidence in the company if they saw such a mess in his office every day.This option does not involve the chairman managing or controlling others' impressions of himself.Instead, he is criticizing manager Chen for his office mess.\n\nC) After hearing his classmates secretly say bad things about him, Lin couldn't help but go up and beat him.This option does not involve the classmates managing or controlling others' impressions of themselves.Instead, they are saying bad things about Lin, and he reacts by beating them.\nXiao Li did not make any preparations for his appearance, clothing, or hairstyle before the interview, as he does not care about managing or controlling others' impressions of himself. He is not concerned with presenting himself in a way that is appropriate to the current social situation or interpersonal context, and is not worried about how others judge him.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
