thwart those expectations.However, the context does not mention anything about people intentionally trying to deceive the surveyor.This option is not supported by the given information.\n\nC) This option states that many opinion surveyors have no expectations whatsoever regarding the answers of people who respond to surveys.However, the context does not provide any information about the surveyors' expectations.This option is not supported by the given information.\nThis option implies that the responses of opinion-survey participants are not affected by their perceptions of the surveyor's expectations, even when those perceptions are accurate. Contrary to the context, individuals do not typically provide responses they think the surveyor wants to receive. Hence, this option contradicts the provided details.\n\nGiven the evaluation, the accurate response is not D) The answers of opinion-survey respondents can be influenced by beliefs about the surveyor's expectations even if those beliefs are unfounded.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
